=> Important Difference – Local Merge vs Pull Request Merge

    -> Old local workflow:

        Feature branch
            ->
        git checkout main
            ->
        git merge feature-branch
            ->
        git push origin main


    -> Collaborative workflow:

        Feature branch
            ->
        Push feature branch
            ->
        Create Pull Request
            ->
        Review
            ->
        Approval
            ->
        Merge Pull Request
            ->
        main


    -> For a protected collaborative repository, prefer the Pull Request workflow.

    -> Do not normally use:

        git checkout main
        git merge developer-branch
        git push origin main

    -> because this bypasses the normal Pull Request review workflow.


=> Common Issues and Resolutions

    -> Issue – Not a Git Repository

        -> Observation:

            fatal: not a git repository
            (or any of the parent directories): .git

        -> Cause:
            -> Git command was executed outside the repository folder.

        -> Resolution:

            cd D:\Vinay_git_repo\core_Java
            -> Move into the actual repository.


            git status
            -> Verify the repository.


    -> Issue – Author Identity Unknown

        -> Observation:

            Author identity unknown

        -> Cause:
            -> Git username and email were not configured.

        -> Resolution:

            git config user.name "Akansha"
            -> Configure local Git username.


            git config user.email "akansha-email@example.com"
            -> Configure local Git email.


    -> Issue – Permission Denied While Pushing

        -> Observation:

            Permission to Vinay8386/core_Java.git denied to Akansha8386.
            HTTP 403

        -> Cause:
            -> Akansha is authenticated but does not have write permission to the repository.

        -> Resolution:
            -> Vinay adds Akansha8386 as a repository collaborator.
            -> Akansha accepts the invitation.
            -> Retry the push.


    -> Issue – GitHub CLI Not Found

        -> Observation:

            'gh' is not recognized as an internal or external command.

        -> Cause:
            -> GitHub CLI is not installed.

        -> Resolution:

            winget install --id GitHub.cli
            -> Install GitHub CLI.


            gh --version
            -> Verify installation.


    -> Issue – GitHub CLI Not Authenticated

        -> Resolution:

            gh auth login
            -> Authenticate GitHub CLI.


            gh auth status
            -> Verify the active GitHub account.


    -> Issue – Merge Is Blocked

        -> Observation:

            Review required
            Merging is blocked
            At least 1 approving review is required

        -> Meaning:
            -> The repository Ruleset is working correctly.

        -> Resolution:
            -> Required reviewer must approve the Pull Request.
            -> After approval, the developer can merge.


    -> Issue – Local Main and Remote Main Have Diverged

        -> Observation:

            Your branch and 'origin/main' have diverged.

        -> Cause:
            -> Local main and remote main contain different commits.

        -> Resolution:

            git pull origin main
            -> Downloads and integrates the remote changes.


        -> Resolve conflicts if Git reports any conflicts.


    -> Issue – Push Rejected Because Local Branch Is Behind

        -> Observation:

            Updates were rejected because the tip of your current branch is behind.

        -> Cause:
            -> Remote branch contains commits that local branch does not contain.

        -> Resolution:

            git pull origin <branch-name>
            -> Download the latest remote branch changes.


            git push
            -> Push after resolving any required conflicts.


    -> Issue – Nothing Added to Commit

        -> Observation:

            nothing added to commit but untracked files present

        -> Cause:
            -> Files were changed but were not staged.

        -> Resolution:

            git add .
            -> Stage all changes.


            git commit -m "Commit message"
            -> Commit the staged changes.


    -> Issue – Wrong Branch Name

        -> Observation:

            merge: feature_branch - not something we can merge

        -> Cause:
            -> The specified branch does not exist.

        -> Resolution:

            git branch
            -> Check the exact local branch names.


            git branch -r
            -> Check the exact remote branch names.


